file-exact render was killed after… - raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.forwarding-six-full-resolution-diagnostic-pngs — Forwarding six full-resolution diagnostic PNGs through the image viewer… - raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.grade-sky-py-reported-zero-pairs-on-a-normal — `grade_sky.py` reported zero pairs on a normal recursive batch output… - raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.knowledge-context-rejects-a-completed-work — knowledge.context rejects a completed work record even when a follow-up… - raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.re-running-stage-dumps-into-an-explicit-tmp — Re-running stage dumps into an explicit `/tmp` diagnostic directory was… - raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.the-full-batch-process-stopped-at-the-execution — The full batch process stopped at the execution harness's ~30-second… - raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.the-unit-tests-that-pinned-the-da23c5f-near — The unit tests that pinned the da23c5f near-white anchor rule were kept… - raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.while-proposing-the-follow-on-work-record-a — While proposing the follow-on work record, a dense inline MCP payload… - raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.while-running-three-targeted-rust-tests-i — While running three targeted Rust tests I passed multiple test filters…

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.collated-8-papercuts-from-lege-ecosystem [about akr]
        Collated 8 papercuts from /mnt/Samsung980_1TB/Rust-projects on 2026-08-13 (D-030). Each source key is also in the collated slot, which is the dedup set for the next run; the sisters were read and never written. ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem.papercut.while-proposing-the-jbig2-smask-preservation [about akr] While proposing the JBIG2 SMask preservation work record, source citations with start_line/end_line were rejected because AKR also requires exact start_byte/end_byte. The proposal schema does not make that coupled range requirement obvious at authoring time; I retried with path-level citations. ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.after-completing-all-g1-g7-children-revising [about akr] After completing all G1-G7 children, revising the spatial track from active to completed was refused because active normative records legitimately depend on the track and the validator treated the resulting completed revision as a superseded target (`slot depends_on may not reference ... /2, which is superseded`). A completed planning prerequisite should remain satisfiable, or the diagnostic should identify the exact dependent that requires repointing. ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.completing-sound-acoustic-studio-and-walk-test [about akr] Completing sound-acoustic-studio-and-walk-test was refused because its inherited part_of relation still targets superseded sound-design/1 even though context also derives it under /2. The child must be revised to the current parent before completion; superseding a track should ideally retarget or clearly disposition child parentage. ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.completing-sound-source-profile-and-lod-audit [about akr] Completing sound-source-profile-and-lod-audit failed because its recovered part_of relations still included terminal sound-design/1 alongside the current track, even though the context bundle had already dispositioned it into sound-design/2. Completion required a relation-only revision first. ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-revise-activates-a-proposed [about akr] knowledge.revise activates a proposed constraint cleanly, but a follow-up revision using `retired_claims` (with or without replacement claims) emits malformed-source parser diagnostics such as unclosed brackets and `constraint has no slot claim`. The API appears to serialize claim retirement incorrectly, preventing removal of a now-false live-counterexample claim. ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-search-could-not-refresh-or-use-the [about akr] knowledge.search could not refresh or use the ledger index because the cache was built without FTS5, forcing direct reads of already-known record keys for gameplay prioritization. ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.while-proposing-a-work-record-i-used-a-natural [about akr] While proposing a work record I used a natural `summary` slot and had to retry after schema rejection; surfacing the valid kind-specific slots in the proposal tool description or accepting `summary` as an alias would avoid this round trip. ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.while-recording-an-unplanned-completed [about akr] While recording an unplanned completed integration slice, knowledge.propose did not surface the required `work.intent` slot until validation rejected the first write; including kind-specific required slots in the tool schema or error-free template would avoid the retry.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.collated-9-papercuts-from-lege-ecosystem [about akr]
        Collated 9 papercuts from /mnt/Samsung980_1TB/Rust-projects on 2026-08-12 (D-030). Each source key is also in the collated slot, which is the dedup set for the next run; the sisters were read and never written. ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem.papercut.knowledge-get-did-not-display-a-work-record-s [about akr] knowledge.get did not display a work record's acceptance checks even at canonical detail, so knowledge.complete had to fail once to reveal the four check IDs needed for evidence mapping. ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem.papercut.while-creating-ocr-work-records-from-a [about akr] While creating OCR work records from a registered source, using the apparent @source.<id> derived_from form produced AKR-L001. The tool could make the source-vs-record citation distinction clearer in relation errors; papercut logging also required a namespace only after the first call failed. ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem.papercut.while-creating-the-auto-toc-work-record [about akr] While creating the auto-TOC work record, `knowledge.propose` accepted a `topic` argument in its API schema but rejected it at validation because planning kinds cannot use topics. The schema could make that kind-specific restriction visible before submission. ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-start-foregrounded-the-blender [about akr] knowledge.start foregrounded the Blender authority decision, but knowledge.context rejects decisions as goals; the handoff could expose the nearest live milestone/track alongside the decision to avoid a failed orientation call. ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.on-akr-0-3-0-for-windows-knowledge-start [about akr] On AKR 0.3.0 for Windows, knowledge.start ignored budget_tokens 1400, assembled about 2116 tokens, then withheld the entire handoff at the 2000-token cap. A later knowledge.context request at 1850 returned a bundle labeled about 4345 tokens, so budget and hard-limit behavior were inconsistent and required multiple slow retries. ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.while-importing-a-connected-sound-design-record [about akr] While importing a connected sound-design record batch, knowledge.propose reported nested validation failures only after each write attempt; a dry-run/schema-introspection mode for slots and reference heads would prevent cascaded retries. One policy also accepts `rationale`, not the otherwise common `context` slot. ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.knowledge-start-withheld-a-6440-token [about akr] knowledge.start withheld a ~6440-token orientation bundle despite a requested 18000-token budget because of an internal 2000-token hard limit; discovering the governing goal therefore requires a separate search/context round trip. ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.orienting-on-this-project-through-the-knowledge [about akr] Orienting on this project through the knowledge.* MCP tools failed at the first step: knowledge.start truncated at a 2000-token hard limit even with budget_tokens=1800 (estimated 3245, continuation null, no way to page), and knowledge.search truncated at 1000 tokens with 20 results. Both returned only a truncation notice with zero usable content, so the sanctioned fallback (AGENTS.md section 10) of reading .akr/records/**/*.akr and docs/generated/ directly was the only route to a project summary. A continuation token, or honouring budget_tokens above the hard limit, would make the tools usable on a ledger this size. ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.while-repairing-phase-4l-evidence-chronology [about akr] While repairing Phase 4L evidence chronology, knowledge.revise returned the completed work revision to proposed even though the call explicitly passed state="completed". A follow-up knowledge.complete restored the intended terminal state; the tool documentation and project gotcha both say re-passing state should preserve it.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.completing-a-milestone-failed-because-a
        Completing a milestone failed because a downstream depends_on edge treated completed work like abandonment, forcing agents to remove the satisfied dependency and manufacture lifecycle revisions. Completion should satisfy depends_on while preserving the edge as provenance.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.evidence-recorded-after-tests-but-before
        Evidence recorded after tests but before  pointed at the parent commit, so the newly committed completed work immediately failed AKR-R022 as evidence predating its content. The change protocol needs a supported two-phase completion flow or evidence tied to the prepared implementation tree instead of an unknowable future commit.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.i-tried-assuming-get-supported-a-source
        I tried , assuming get supported a source rendering mode; --format is only the global text/json selector. The get help could make raw-record inspection guidance explicit for agents closing acceptance checks.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.knowledge-context-guidance-suggests-reading-a [about akr]
        knowledge.context guidance suggests reading a task record by goal, but it rejects papercut records and only then tells the caller to use knowledge.get. The context API documentation should state its planning-record restriction up front.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.knowledge-context-rejects-completed-work-goals [about akr]
        knowledge.context rejects completed work goals with AKR-X002 even when the repository protocol says to call context with the exact planning key; corrective follow-up needs a new work record before the prior bundle can be inspected.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.knowledge-search-detects-a-stale-index-but
        knowledge.search detects a stale index but continues serving it, so agents repeatedly receive known-old planning results until a human runs `akr build`. Search should safely refresh or fall back to current source data before returning results.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.revising-a-sealed-record-through-the-supported
        Revising a sealed record through the supported knowledge.revise path changes its old revision to superseded and causes knowledge.validate to report AKR-R051 until rebuild, while ops documentation says lifecycle writes should produce AKR-R052. This makes an authorized lifecycle transition look like sealed-content tampering; distinguish it or document the exact rebuild boundary.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.running-rustfmt-directly-on-akr-s-rust-2024 [about rustfmt]
        Running rustfmt directly on AKR's Rust 2024 files defaulted to an older edition and rejected existing let-chains; the non-obvious required invocation is rustfmt --edition 2024.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.strict-clippy-for-the-new-gui-crate-promoted
        Strict clippy for the new GUI crate promoted more than 200 existing missing-docs warnings from the in-progress ingest APIs and obscured the one GUI lint. A target-scoped lint profile or temporary ingest-specific allowance would keep unrelated dependency warnings from swamping focused checks.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.the-akr-mcp-transport-closed-on-explain-and [about akr]
        The AKR MCP transport closed on explain and propose calls, forcing a CLI fallback. The CLI described --from as a record body but rejected plain prose because a required slot declaration was still needed; the help should name the accepted slot-list shape explicitly.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.the-cli-help-advertises-edit-for-propose-and
        The CLI help advertises --edit for propose and revise, but this build rejects it as unavailable; the documented path caused an avoidable failed write before falling back to --from.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.the-repository-instructions-direct-agents-to [about akr]
        The repository instructions direct agents to use `knowledge.start`/`knowledge.context`, but the installed `akr.exe` has no `knowledge` CLI command; the MCP ledger tools were required instead. The documented CLI and installed binary are out of sync.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.while-beginning-a-change-transaction-the
        While beginning a change transaction, the natural kind 'feature' was rejected because the accepted spelling is the undocumented Conventional Commit abbreviation 'feat'; the error recovers well, but help or aliasing would avoid the retry.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.while-checking-akr-mcp-without-default-features [about akr]
        While checking akr-mcp without default features, the differential harness first used a stale default-feature target/debug/akr unless that CLI binary was rebuilt explicitly; after rebuilding correctly, two knowledge.start fallback tests still fail because the non-FTS validated-head path omits coverage and workspace_fallback metadata. The budget/pagination tests themselves pass in that configuration.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.while-locating-the-non-fts-start-and [about fff]
        While locating the non-FTS start and differential harness code, the first FFF multi_grep call failed because its transport closed; rg was the only usable fallback.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.while-running-the-workspace-suite-on-windows
        While running the workspace suite on Windows, `akr-cli`'s transcript harness unconditionally spawned `sh` for its limited `sed` directives and failed with program not found. Implement those fixture rewrites in Rust/PowerShell-independent code or skip them with an explicit platform diagnostic.

        ## AKR @akr.papercut.writing-several-evidence-and-lifecycle-records
        Writing several evidence and lifecycle records repeated full Git-history work and a post-write session reload, turning small ledger mutations into minute-scale operations. Batch Git facts by ledger file, avoid the redundant reload, and provide atomic bulk evidence.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.a-final-ripgrep-line-number-lookup-embedded-a
        A final ripgrep line-number lookup embedded a double-quoted regex inside a double-quoted PowerShell command, so the quotes were consumed and rg reported an unclosed group; single-quote regex literals in PowerShell.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.a-recursive-api-scan-used-the-common-unix-style
        A recursive API scan used the common Unix-style 'rg ... src/*.rs' form, but PowerShell passed the glob literally and ripgrep rejected it; use 'rg ... src -g *.rs' on this Windows workspace.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.adding-the-evidence-gui-binary-made-the-readme
        Adding the evidence-gui binary made the README's existing 'cargo run -- ...' commands ambiguous; the smoke-test seed failed until the package declared evidence as default-run.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.akr-mcp-timed-out-after-65s-on-the-first
        AKR MCP timed out after 65s on the first knowledge call; the CLI is kr start / kr propose, not kr knowledge start. Used the CLI for the rest of the session.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.akr-propose-from-help-says-a-file-holding-the
        'akr propose --from' help says a file holding the record body but does not show the required parseable wrapper; passing plain prose failed with AKR-C031 instead of identifying the expected body grammar.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.codegraph-explore-hung-16-minutes-on-a-12-file
        codegraph_explore hung ~16 minutes on a 12-file query (Command/Cases/Workspace/require_case). Prefer node/search/read over explore on this workspace.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.i-passed-scope-terms-as-path-src-gui-winsafe-rs [about akr]
        I passed scope terms as "path src/gui/winsafe.rs" to knowledge.propose, copying the `path "..."` form the generated views render, and it was accepted silently — producing scope `path "path src/gui/winsafe.rs"`, a glob that can never match a file, so the records would never have gone stale when winsafe.rs changed. Nothing validates that a scope glob is well-formed or warns that it currently matches zero paths. A warning when a path term matches nothing in the worktree would have caught this at propose time instead of three records later.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.knowledge-explain-crashed-with-akr-x099 [about akr]
        knowledge.explain crashed with AKR-X099 (internal) for both `decision` and `constraint` after knowledge.propose rejected my slots with AKR-T002. The propose error names the bad slot but not the valid ones, and explain -- the documented way to find them -- is exactly what fails, so I had to read .akr/records/*.akr by hand to learn that a decision uses `decision` plus `claim` blocks and has no `rationale` or `note` slot. Suggest AKR-T002 list the kind's valid slots inline.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.knowledge-propose-returns-lock-stale-true-on [about akr]
        knowledge.propose returns lock_stale:true on every write but does not refresh akr.lock, so a later knowledge.validate fails with AKR-R052 ("akr.lock has no hash for <the record I just wrote>"). The fix is `akr lock --update`, but nothing in the propose result or the diagnostic says so, and AGENTS.md's "never hand-edit .akr/" made me hesitant to touch the lock at all. Suggest either refreshing the lock as part of propose, or having AKR-R052 name `akr lock --update` as the remedy.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.ran-knowledge-context-goal-on-a-project-whose [about akr]
        Ran knowledge.context --goal on a project whose ledger held only the namespace stub in project.akr; it failed with AKR-X001 "does not resolve to a record" rather than saying the ledger is empty. On a fresh project that reads as a broken tool call. A distinct message ("no records yet; start with knowledge.propose") would tell an agent to author the first record instead of retrying with different goal strings.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.the-agents-protocol-names-commands-as-knowledge
        The AGENTS protocol names commands as knowledge.context, but this PowerShell environment only exposes the akr executable; the first required context call failed until translated to 'akr context'.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.the-first-gui-smoke-screenshot-used
        The first GUI smoke screenshot used CopyFromScreen on the WinSafe window bounds, but another terminal occluded those bounds and the saved image showed the covering window; foreground the target or use PrintWindow for reliable native UI capture.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.video-transcriber-mcp-looks-like-a-reusable
        video-transcriber-mcp looks like a reusable Whisper crate on lib.rs but it is an MCP/YouTube downloader (yt-dlp, axum, REMOTE_WHISPER_URL). The reusable engine is whisper-rs. Putting whisper-rs behind a Cargo feature still gets compiled by the repo's cargo clippy --all-features.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.a-combined-inspection-command-printed-the
        A combined inspection command printed the requested posctl section but its leading rg alternation was mangled into an unclosed regex by nested quoting. Prefer separate simple rg commands instead of a quoted alternation when inspecting PowerShell output.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.adding-sql-migration-0015-also-requires
        Adding SQL migration 0015 also requires updating the handwritten MIGRATIONS registry and schema-version assertions in store.rs; a missed registry entry leaves tests without the new columns.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.agents-md-names-knowledge-validate-but-this
        AGENTS.md names knowledge.validate, but this workspace exposes no such executable or PowerShell command. kr check is the available validation command and completed with no diagnostics.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.akr-get-for-the-active-indonesia-formatting-tax
        akr get for the active Indonesia formatting/tax work record timed out without output on a small local knowledge base. Direct record inspection was needed to recover the acceptance-check IDs.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.akr-mcp-server-failed-to-connect-at-session [about akr]
        AKR MCP server failed to connect at session start, so knowledge.start/context were unavailable; used the akr CLI instead.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.akr-propose-from-describes-a-record-body-source
        akr propose --from describes a record body source, but rejects one without an akr header and complete record; source-format expectations need documenting.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.akr-propose-from-describes-its-input-as-an-akr
        akr propose --from describes its input as an AKR slot-list fragment, but the obvious 'intent: text' form from akr explain failed with a parser error and neither command output showed a valid fragment example.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.akr-propose-from-expects-a-complete-akr-record
        akr propose --from expects a complete AKR record rather than the prose body described by its help text, so a plain scratch note is rejected as unparsable. Show an input example or clarify the required envelope.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.akr-search-kind-milestone-returned-zero-results
        akr search --kind milestone returned zero results without explaining that --kind is unsupported; use direct record lookup or plain search instead.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.build-release-pertama-saya-beri-timeout-1-detik
        Build release pertama saya beri timeout 1 detik untuk mencoba memperoleh cell proses, tetapi shell_command membunuh proses setelah minimum sekitar 5 detik alih-alih mengembalikan handle; build harus diulang dengan timeout panjang. Dokumentasi tool sebaiknya menjelaskan bahwa proses tidak otomatis menjadi resumable.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.cargo-test-workspace-warns-that-keypad-lab-and
        cargo test --workspace warns that keypad-lab and back-office both publish an example named screens, which collides in target/debug/examples and may become a hard Cargo error. Rename one example before a future toolchain upgrade.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.concurrent-akr-evidence-add-processes-both
        Concurrent akr evidence add processes both reported success while updating the same evidence file, but one record was lost due to a write race. AKR mutations must be serialized or the CLI should lock/reject concurrent writers.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.pencarian-rg-untuk-contoh-record-akr-gagal
        Pencarian rg untuk contoh record AKR gagal karena quoting regex bertingkat pada shell PowerShell; perlu mengulang dengan single quote. Contoh perintah PowerShell di dokumentasi AKR akan mengurangi trial-and-error.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.pencarian-rg-untuk-contoh-record-akr-gagal-2
        Pencarian rg untuk contoh record AKR gagal karena quoting regex bertingkat pada shell PowerShell; perlu mengulang dengan single quote. Contoh perintah PowerShell di dokumentasi AKR akan mengurangi trial-and-error.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.porting-a-12-document-40kb-source-planning
        Porting a 12-document, ~40KB-source planning corpus by hand-authoring .akr directly (rather than akr import) worked well but gave no tooling checkpoint between 'wrote N records' and 'akr check' at the end — no per-file dry-run/lint equivalent to import --dry-run for hand-authored source. A lightweight 'akr check <file>' scoped to one new file would let an agent validate incrementally while drafting a large batch instead of writing all ~80 records before the first syntax feedback.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.powershell-quoting-turned-an-rg-cargo-lock
        PowerShell quoting turned an rg Cargo.lock pattern with embedded double quotes into an invalid regex; use single-quoted patterns for manifest searches on Windows.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.project-instructions-name-knowledge-context-but
        Project instructions name knowledge.context, but this workspace exposes only akr context; the documented wrapper is unavailable.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.relation-domain-range-e-g-resolves-work
        Relation domain/range (e.g. resolves: work/decision/observation/evidence -> question, not the reverse) isn't spelled out in exemplar.akr or the migration/data-model prose I skimmed; I placed 'resolves' on the question record first and had to grep spec/tables/vocabulary.json directly to find the correct direction. A one-line relation-direction cheat sheet in docs/02-data-model.md §7 (or a hint in the akr-source prompt's relations section) would have saved a check-fail round trip.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.saat-memulai-pekerjaan-packaging-pos-protokol
        Saat memulai pekerjaan packaging POS, protokol menyebut perintah knowledge.context tetapi wrapper itu tidak tersedia di PowerShell; perlu memakai padanan akr context. Dokumentasikan pemetaan nama perintah atau sediakan wrapper lintas-shell.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.saat-menulis-acceptance-record-packaging-saya
        Saat menulis acceptance record packaging, saya memakai method test secara intuitif tetapi schema hanya menerima manual, command, atau observation; pesan error membantu, namun daftar nilai valid di akr explain work akan mencegah retry.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.smoke-test-paket-sebagai-command-powershell
        Smoke test paket sebagai command PowerShell inline yang panjang ditolak oleh kebijakan terminal walaupun targetnya hanya scratch; saya harus memindahkannya ke file .agent/scratch lalu menjalankan file itu. Pesan kebijakan sebaiknya menunjukkan konstruksi mana yang memicu penolakan.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.terminating-a-long-running-cargo-test-left-its
        Terminating a long-running cargo test left its Windows test executable alive and locked, so the next link failed with Permission denied; stop the specific pos_reporting test process after terminating a yielded cargo cell.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.the-agents-protocol-names-knowledge-propose-but
        The AGENTS protocol names knowledge.propose, but the installed CLI has no knowledge subcommand; the retry had to discover the top-level command form. Document the exact AKR CLI mapping.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.the-bundled-pdftoppm-cmd-was-discoverable-with
        The bundled pdftoppm.cmd was discoverable with Get-Command but failed with 'The system cannot find the path specified' when rendering a generated PDF; the wrapper's target path appears stale and needs repair or clearer diagnostics.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.the-evidence-add-examples-use-a-bare-key-but
        The evidence-add examples use a bare <key>, but project validation requires a declared dot-delimited namespace; the first attempt used an intuitive unqualified evidence name and was rejected. An example with a qualified project key would prevent the retry.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.the-first-multi-file-apply-patch-missed-the
        The first multi-file apply_patch missed the escaped newline in delivery-display's help string, so the all-or-nothing patch had to be retried with that line isolated. Escaped multiline literals make broad textual patches brittle.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.the-full-indonesian-workspace-test-run-timed
        The full Indonesian workspace test run timed out during its first compile and closed the test pipe; after rerunning from cache, the known Windows crash_harness subprocess tests failed nondeterministically while all preceding suites passed. The harness needs a documented longer timeout and more deterministic child-process synchronization.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.the-indonesian-packaging-script-forced-a-full
        The Indonesian packaging script forced a full release rebuild via CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_DEBUG=0 and MinGW's winit build-script link failed with an empty linker diagnostic, despite earlier release builds succeeding. This makes package regeneration slow and the failure opaque.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.the-pos-smoke-command-assumed-cargo-test-had
        The POS smoke command assumed cargo test had emitted target/debug/posctl.exe, but only the hashed test executable existed. Use cargo run (or build the named binary first) for command-level smoke tests.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.the-requested-restaurant-post-sources-path-did
        The requested restaurant-post/sources path did not exist; the material is under restaurant-pos/sources, making the intended planning inputs easy to miss.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.the-windows-crash-harness-repeatedly-reports
        The Windows crash harness repeatedly reports claimed outbox jobs as vanished at BeforeOutboxDelivery/AfterOutboxDelivery, even when run with --test-threads=1; the four sale/rollup crash tests pass. The existing lease-aware outbox semantics and harness expectation appear out of sync and need a separate fix.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.tried-akr-validate-per-agents-md-cli-rejects-it
        Tried akr validate per Agents.md; CLI rejects it as unknown (AKR-C001). Used akr context --goal kitchen.milestone.phase2-inventory-and-costing and akr get kitchen.req.inventory-and-recipe-invariants/1 instead. Also codegraph is not initialized in restaurant-pos or the workspace root, so inventory review used file reads.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.two-policy-records-with-the-same-topic-and
        Two policy records with the same topic and overlapping scope silently produced AKR-R002 only at 'akr check' time, not at write time. When hand-authoring many records in one batch (as opposed to one 'akr propose' at a time), a lint/fmt-time warning for topic collisions across the whole workspace would surface this before running the full check pass.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.while-adding-completion-evidence-i-passed-the
        While adding completion evidence, I passed the work record reference as kr evidence add's positional key. That argument is the new evidence record's dot-delimited key, not the work being evidenced; the relationship is supplied later by acceptance checks/complete.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.while-adding-finalized-source-guards-to
        While adding finalized-source guards to migration 0017, I added a second daily_signoff_no_delete trigger even though the same migration already recreated it after rebuilding the table. Fresh database tests caught the duplicate trigger name; keep guards adjacent to the table rebuild or use unique names.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.while-auditing-indonesian-quantity-formatting-a
        While auditing Indonesian quantity formatting, a double-quoted rg regex containing PowerShell's property-access pattern was parsed by PowerShell before rg and failed. Use single-quoted regexes or simpler searches in PowerShell examples.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.while-formatting-a-changed-ui-file-i-invoked
        While formatting a changed UI file, I invoked rustfmt with a workspace-root-prefixed path after changing into the restaurant-pos subdirectory, so the formatter missed the file even though subsequent checks passed. Keep command paths relative to the selected workdir.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.while-registering-the-approved-audited
        While registering the approved audited-inventory work, kr propose --from described the input as a record body but rejected plain intent prose because it actually requires a typed record fragment; the help should show the required fragment syntax.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.while-searching-migration-sql-on-windows
        While searching migration SQL on Windows, passing a Unix-style glob path (migrations/*.sql) directly to rg is treated as a literal invalid filename. Search the directory and use rg's -g '*.sql' filter instead.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.while-selecting-several-rust-tests-cargo-test
        While selecting several Rust tests, cargo test accepts only one positional TESTNAME filter, so multiple fully-qualified test names are rejected. Use one shared substring, separate invocations, or run the whole library target.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.while-wiring-the-inventory-editor
        While wiring the inventory editor, TextFieldState::apply returns bool, so expression-form match arms conflict with block arms returning unit. Wrap apply calls in blocks or discard the return value explicitly.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.after-completing-all-g1-g7-children-revising [about akr]
        After completing all G1-G7 children, revising the spatial track from active to completed was refused because active normative records legitimately depend on the track and the validator treated the resulting completed revision as a superseded target (`slot depends_on may not reference ... /2, which is superseded`). A completed planning prerequisite should remain satisfiable, or the diagnostic should identify the exact dependent that requires repointing.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.after-knowledge-revise-changed-an-existing [about akr]
        After knowledge.revise changed an existing milestone revision from proposed to ready in place, a second revise with the same base revision and state active created a new revision in proposed state instead of activating it. This repeated on revisions 3 and 4; completing directly from ready worked.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.akr-build-fails-on-this-working-tree-with-error [about akr]
        `akr build` fails on this working tree with "error[AKR-I002]: cannot write revisions: CHECK constraint failed: method IS NULL OR method IN ('manual','command','observation','instrumented')". It succeeds against HEAD, so one of the uncommitted record edits in .akr/records/saveyourskin/ carries a method value outside that set. The error names neither the record nor the offending value, which makes it hard to find; reporting the key and method would fix that. Consequence: the lock cannot be refreshed, so knowledge.validate reports AKR-R052 for every newly written record.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.akr-check-akr-build-akr-lock-update-each-took
        akr check / akr build / akr lock --update each took >120s (timed out the 120s bash default and had to background) on saveyourskin, a ~360-record, ~330-commit repo -- ancestry-facts computation (git merge-base --is-ancestor per evidence citation, per D-016/D-028) seems to dominate. Every write-then-validate cycle during a large port session pays this cost repeatedly; a cached/batched ancestry check (e.g. one 'git rev-list --ancestry-path' walk instead of O(citations) merge-base calls) would make interactive porting sessions much faster.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.akr-check-build-validate-the-whole-ledger-with
        akr check/build validate the whole ledger with no way to scope to just the records I'm adding; a pre-existing AKR-R022 failure in milestones.akr (unrelated real-engine work, not part of this markdown-porting task) blocked akr build and akr check --views-current for my 300+ new records even though they were themselves clean, and I had no flag like --only <path> to confirm my additions in isolation.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.akr-mcp-server-failed-to-connect-used-the-akr [about akr]
        AKR MCP server failed to connect; used the akr CLI for start/context/propose/validate.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.authoring-a-new-track-s-records-cost-three [about akr]
        Authoring a new track's records cost three failed writes to discover relation/slot rules that aren't visible from the propose schema: a `constraint` rejects the `note` slot (planning kinds only, D-026), an `observation` may not declare `supported_by`, and a `milestone` may not declare `implements` (both V-005). The tool description lists relation names generically, so the per-kind restrictions only surface as errors after a full record body is composed. Either the propose schema's relations field could name the allowed relations per kind, or the V-005 error could suggest the nearest legal relation (`derived_from` in both of my cases). Separately, an `observation`'s `observed_at` requires a 40-hex commit while the kind's description just says "observed_at", so an ISO date is a natural first guess and fails with a parse cascade of three diagnostics.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.both-fff-find-files-and-multi-grep-returned [about FFF]
        Both FFF find_files and multi_grep returned `Transport closed` while locating the active stair gait reference assets, so I had to fall back to rg for the mandated discovery step.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.both-find-files-and-multi-grep-failed-with [about FFF]
        Both find_files and multi_grep failed with `Transport closed` while beginning the sound integration audit, so discovery had to fall back to narrow rg searches.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.check-world-freshness-ps1-cannot-pass-for-any
        check_world_freshness.ps1 cannot pass for any world that has object instances: it exports into target/world-freshness/<world>, and sys_castle_tool normalize resolves the object catalog by walking ancestors for object_library/library.json, which does not exist outside the assets tree. It fails with "world greyhaven has object instances but no ancestor object_library/library.json". Verified pre-existing — the pre-rebuild committed world fails identically. Fix is probably to pass the library path explicitly to normalize rather than infer it from the output location.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.completing-sound-acoustic-studio-and-walk-test [about akr]
        Completing sound-acoustic-studio-and-walk-test was refused because its inherited part_of relation still targets superseded sound-design/1 even though context also derives it under /2. The child must be revised to the current parent before completion; superseding a track should ideally retarget or clearly disposition child parentage.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.completing-sound-source-profile-and-lod-audit [about akr]
        Completing sound-source-profile-and-lod-audit failed because its recovered part_of relations still included terminal sound-design/1 alongside the current track, even though the context bundle had already dispositioned it into sound-design/2. Completion required a relation-only revision first.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.fff-content-search-transport-closed-twice [about fff]
        FFF content search transport closed twice during M4 source lookup, so discovery had to fall back to rg after the required FFF-first calls.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.fff-find-files-failed-twice-with-transport [about FFF]
        FFF find_files failed twice with `Transport closed` during required repository discovery, including a single-call retry, so the task had to fall back to rg.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.fff-find-files-transport-closed-while-locating [about FFF]
        FFF find_files transport closed while locating the user-directed Sources/current-plan-80626.md, so discovery had to fall back to direct read-only shell inspection.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-context-accepted-budget-tokens-18000 [about akr]
        knowledge.context accepted budget_tokens=18000 but then withheld a 16208-token bundle because of an undocumented 4000-token response ceiling; callers should be told/capped before the expensive assembly.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-context-rejected-a-valid-key-revision [about akr]
        knowledge.context rejected a valid @key/revision reference even though knowledge.get accepts that canonical reference form; it required the bare logical key, making goal resumption take two retries. The context tool/docs could state or normalize this syntax.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-get-rendered-a-work-record-s-main [about akr]
        knowledge.get rendered a work record's main slot without naming it, so a faithful knowledge.revise first tried `goal`; the schema only then revealed the slot is `intent`. Exposing slot names in body/canonical output would avoid a failed write attempt.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-propose-accepted-an-implements [about akr]
        knowledge.propose accepted an `implements` relation to a work record at the call boundary and only later rejected it under V-005; relation target-kind constraints in the tool description would make completed-slice recording single-pass.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-propose-accepted-observation-method [about akr]
        knowledge.propose accepted observation method `inspection` and wrote a verified revision, but `akr build` rejects that stored historical revision because the index CHECK allows only manual/command/observation/instrumented. Revising the head to `instrumented` cannot repair the now-invalid sealed revision, so write-time validation and the index schema need the same enum or a supported repair path.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-revise-activates-a-proposed [about akr]
        knowledge.revise activates a proposed constraint cleanly, but a follow-up revision using `retired_claims` (with or without replacement claims) emits malformed-source parser diagnostics such as unclosed brackets and `constraint has no slot claim`. The API appears to serialize claim retirement incorrectly, preventing removal of a now-false live-counterexample claim.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-search-could-not-refresh-or-use-the [about akr]
        knowledge.search could not refresh or use the ledger index because the cache was built without FTS5, forcing direct reads of already-known record keys for gameplay prioritization.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-start-foregrounded-the-blender [about akr]
        knowledge.start foregrounded the Blender authority decision, but knowledge.context rejects decisions as goals; the handoff could expose the nearest live milestone/track alongside the decision to avoid a failed orientation call.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-supersede-documents-a-new-key-option [about akr]
        knowledge.supersede documents a new_key option, but AKR 0.1 rejects every different-key supersession with AKR-C004. I had to supersede the existing key in place, which prevents giving a materially changed design ruling a more accurate key.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.on-akr-0-3-0-for-windows-knowledge-start [about akr]
        On AKR 0.3.0 for Windows, knowledge.start ignored budget_tokens 1400, assembled about 2116 tokens, then withheld the entire handoff at the 2000-token cap. A later knowledge.context request at 1850 returned a bundle labeled about 4345 tokens, so budget and hard-limit behavior were inconsistent and required multiple slow retries.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.revising-an-active-decision-s-content [about akr]
        Revising an active decision's content implicitly returned its lifecycle state to proposed, requiring a second state-only revise. Preserving the head state by default, or explicitly warning that omitted state resets it, would avoid an easy accidental deactivation.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.running-the-focused-documentation-audit-as
        Running the focused documentation audit as cargo test --release --test doc_audit failed because Cargo selected no package; the documented reliable invocation needs -p save_your_skin. The focused lane was retried with the explicit package.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.the-first-m6-multi-grep-for-notary-lodging [about FFF]
        The first M6 multi_grep for notary, lodging-warrant, access, and opening symbols failed immediately with `Transport closed`; repository discovery had to fall back to local rg again.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.the-portable-object-library-readme-still [about repository documentation]
        The portable object-library README still instructed `sys_castle_tool object-library`, but that subcommand was removed during the Blender-authority cutover. The actual maintained audit is the focused `sys_assets` release test; the README was corrected.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.the-prescribed-broad-cargo-test-release
        The prescribed broad `cargo test --release --workspace` lane cannot finish green because `tests/doc_audit.rs::agents_cited_doc_paths_exist` cites 34 planning documents that are absent from the repository and not tracked at HEAD; the simulator library itself passed 762 tests before this unrelated integration failure.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.the-repository-provides-only-an-elf-cargo [about cargo-checker]
        `rg --files` surfaced only the extensionless ELF `cargo-checker`, so the first Windows check attempt went through WSL and failed. A working `cargo-checker.exe` exists at the repository root but is omitted from that discovery path; documenting or tracking the platform pair would prevent the false negative.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.the-repository-s-check-bat-documents-and [about cargo-checker]
        The repository's check.bat documents and invokes `cargo-checker.exe --workspace --all-targets`, but the available Windows checker rejects `--workspace` as an unexpected argument. I had to inspect the helper interface instead of using the documented workspace check directly.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.two-consecutive-semantic-identical-working [about Blender 5.2 glTF exporter]
        Two consecutive semantic-identical working-castle library rebuilds kept catalog and geometry-report bytes stable but changed several GLB and .blend hashes. The committed outputs validate and render identically, but exporter serialization order should be canonicalized before byte-for-byte rebuild freshness is used for portable object libraries.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.while-importing-a-connected-sound-design-record [about akr]
        While importing a connected sound-design record batch, knowledge.propose reported nested validation failures only after each write attempt; a dry-run/schema-introspection mode for slots and reference heads would prevent cascaded retries. One policy also accepts `rationale`, not the otherwise common `context` slot.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.while-proposing-a-work-record-i-used-a-natural [about akr]
        While proposing a work record I used a natural `summary` slot and had to retry after schema rejection; surfacing the valid kind-specific slots in the proposal tool description or accepting `summary` as an alias would avoid this round trip.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.while-recording-a-completed-work-slice [about akr]
        While recording a completed work slice, knowledge.propose's schema exposed slots as an unconstrained object and did not tell me that work records accept intent/target/note rather than summary; the call failed only after validation. Publishing per-kind slot names in the tool schema or description would avoid the retry.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.while-recording-a-verified-gameplay-video [about akr]
        While recording a verified gameplay-video observation, knowledge.propose parsed a descriptive method containing `15 fps` and punctuation as slot syntax instead of rejecting it as an invalid enum value. The schema should validate/quote the method argument before serializing it.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.while-recording-an-unplanned-completed [about akr]
        While recording an unplanned completed integration slice, knowledge.propose did not surface the required `work.intent` slot until validation rejected the first write; including kind-specific required slots in the tool schema or error-free template would avoid the retry.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.while-removing-37-acknowledged-missing-source [about akr]
        While removing 37 acknowledged missing-source citations, knowledge.get, knowledge.revise, knowledge.explain, and knowledge.validate repeatedly returned Transport closed; the local akr CLI remained healthy and provided the necessary fallback.

        ## bpg-rs @bpg.papercut.a-broad-rg-over-the-cargo-registry-for-zune
        A broad rg over the Cargo registry for zune-jpeg EXIF internals timed out; narrowing to the resolved package directory avoids scanning the full registry.

        ## bpg-rs @bpg.papercut.preparing-the-heic-implementation-commit-akr
        Preparing the HEIC implementation commit, akr context rejected the completed milestone as a goal; the workflow does not identify an obvious context target for post-completion handoff work.

        ## bpg-rs @bpg.papercut.repository-guidance-spells-the-context
        Repository guidance spells the context operation as 'knowledge.context', but only the 'akr' executable is installed; the command mapping is not obvious and the first required context call fails.

        ## bpg-rs @bpg.papercut.running-akr-get-format-json-on-a-small
        Running 'akr get ... --format json' on a small milestone timed out after 14 seconds, while the text form completed; JSON retrieval unexpectedly blocks schema-oriented setup.

        ## bpg-rs @bpg.papercut.task-brief-for-a-historical-port-asked-for-docs
        Task brief for a historical port asked for docs/generated/DECISION-HISTORY.md alongside ROADMAP.md to read as the development story, but this akr 0.1.0 build only implements the roadmap and papercuts view renderers -- decision-history, current-state, active-work, review-required, and open-questions all fail with AKR-E003 'the X renderer arrives with a later phase'. akr build and akr check --views-current silently treat the unimplemented views as vacuously current instead of warning, so the gap is only visible by running akr view <name> directly. Worth a note in the CLI help or check output that these renderers are stubs in 0.1.0.

        ## bpg-rs @bpg.papercut.v-020-s-descendant-commit-freshness-gate-akr
        V-020's descendant-commit freshness gate (AKR-R022) is structurally incompatible with a single-commit historical/bulk port: once the .akr records themselves are committed, that commit becomes the 'last commit that changed the content' for every completed milestone/work record, and no historical evidence (dated before the port, which is the whole point of a historical port) can ever be a descendant of it. akr check --views-current was clean on the working tree before committing the ledger; the same check fails with ~19 AKR-R022 diagnostics immediately after committing, for every completed record with an evidence-backed acceptance check. No amount of re-running akr build fixes it since the evidence commits are fixed historical facts. Possible product answers: exempt records whose source is  from the descendant check, or document that bulk historical imports should land as one commit per original doc/commit to keep evidence descendant-valid, or accept this as an expected one-time 'stale on arrival, re-verify to close' state for historical ports and say so in docs/12-migration.md.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.akr-check-strict-exits-1-on-akr-g004-alone-when
        akr check --strict exits 1 on AKR-G004 alone when watched paths have uncommitted edits during a disposition; lenient is clean. Makes 'akr check is clean' acceptance awkward mid-session before commit.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.akr-import-of-performance-md-dry-run-proposed
        akr import of PERFORMANCE.md --dry-run proposed every section as kind work (including rules and measurements), so manual propose/revise was required for policy/decision/observation disposition.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.akr-mcp-install-setup-akr-mcp-sh-cp-fails-with
        akr-mcp install: setup-akr-mcp.sh cp fails with Text file busy when an MCP client holds the old binary open; atomic mv over a .new file works. setup script should install via rename.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.akr-propose-from-rejects-slot-only-bodies
        akr propose --from rejects slot-only bodies; requires full akr 0.1 project header + record { ... } even though help says 'a file holding the record body'. First attempt failed with AKR-C031.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.akr-view-active-work-current-state-etc-returned
        akr view ACTIVE-WORK/CURRENT-STATE/etc returned AKR-E003 (renderer arrives later) on an intermediate binary while roadmap worked; full akr build needed for other views. Confusing when only roadmap is available.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.cargo-fmt-all-check-fails-on-code-committed-at
        `cargo fmt --all --check` fails on code committed at HEAD (25213f6): jpxl-core/src/{color,dct}.rs, jpxl-encode/src/{lib,resources}.rs, jpxl-encode/src/modular/squeeze.rs, jpxl-encode/src/vardct/gaborish.rs and two blocks in jpxl-bitstream/src/writer.rs all carry pre-existing formatting drift. That makes scripts/ci-akr.sh's third gate red independently of any working-tree change, and it means running `cargo fmt` during ordinary work silently rewrites six files nobody touched -- exactly the hazard AGENTS.md section 10 warns about, now with a standing trigger. Separately, AGENTS.md section 5's documented gate `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` cannot pass by construction: the workspace sets unwrap_used, indexing_slicing and cast_possible_truncation to "warn" and there are 100+ live hits, so -D warnings turns the project's own deliberate lint policy into errors.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.fff-find-files-returned-transport-closed-while [about fff]
        FFF find_files returned `Transport closed` while locating the fresh Phase 8.5 profile and execution-boundary sources, forcing a fallback to precise rg searches. This is a repeat of the earlier Linux optimization-session disconnect.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.fff-grep-transport-closed-while-locating-bench [about fff]
        FFF grep transport closed while locating bench_vardct_rate; the indexed CodeGraph search/node fallback returned the symbol and source immediately.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.fff-grep-transport-closed-while-verifying-the [about fff]
        FFF grep transport closed while verifying the user-provided bpg-rs saliency implementation; precise rg/sed fallback was required.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.fff-multi-grep-again-failed-with-transport [about fff]
        FFF multi_grep again failed with 'Transport closed' while mapping the post-Phase-8.5 quantization/rate-search path, so discovery had to fall back to scoped rg. The repeated disconnect makes the instructed default discovery layer unavailable.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.hybrid-intel-plain-cycles-u-records-cpu-atom
        Hybrid Intel: plain cycles:u records cpu_atom+cpu_core; atom samples can dominate collapsed stacks (vardct-rate first pass looked like only synthetic_rgb8). Always use -e cpu_core/cycles/u and taskset to P-cores for reusable flamegraphs.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.jpxl-bench-fingerprints-outputs-with-fnv-1a-64
        jpxl bench fingerprints outputs with FNV-1a-64, but PERFORMANCE.md baselines require a cryptographic hash of codestream and binary; need --sha256 or a post-pass so promotion is not hand work.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.knowledge-complete-s-cited-evidence-gets-its
        knowledge.complete's cited evidence gets its observed_at commit hash from the current git HEAD at write time, which is the *parent* commit if the record and its evidence are still uncommitted -- so `akr check`/`knowledge.validate` after the eventual `git commit` flags V-020 "evidence predates last content change" even though the evidence genuinely verifies the committed content. Workaround used twice this session: after committing, add a second evidence record (re-running the same cheap check) and re-run knowledge.complete citing it, then `akr build`. A cleaner fix might be an explicit `observed_at` override accepted post-hoc, or docs telling agents to commit code before the propose/evidence/complete sequence rather than after.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.knowledge-propose-documents-observation [about akr]
        knowledge.propose documents observation observed_at as required but does not say it must be a git:<40-hex> locator; passing the natural ISO date 2026-08-11 produced parser errors about a 4-digit commit hash.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.knowledge-propose-says-observation-requires [about akr]
        knowledge.propose says observation requires statement and observed_at, but a verified observation also requires method/source/evidence (V-022); after adding method, the natural accompanying command slot is rejected because observation does not permit command.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.knowledge-start-withheld-a-6440-token [about akr]
        knowledge.start withheld a ~6440-token orientation bundle despite a requested 18000-token budget because of an internal 2000-token hard limit; discovering the governing goal therefore requires a separate search/context round trip.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.opt-f-multiplicity-counters-are-still-only
        Opt-F multiplicity counters are still only listed in PERFORMANCE.md — no feature-gated EncodeStats in policy/encode — so flamegraphs cannot yet separate repeated DCT from expensive DCT.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.orienting-on-this-project-through-the-knowledge [about akr]
        Orienting on this project through the knowledge.* MCP tools failed at the first step: knowledge.start truncated at a 2000-token hard limit even with budget_tokens=1800 (estimated 3245, continuation null, no way to page), and knowledge.search truncated at 1000 tokens with 20 results. Both returned only a truncation notice with zero usable content, so the sanctioned fallback (AGENTS.md section 10) of reading .akr/records/**/*.akr and docs/generated/ directly was the only route to a project summary. A continuation token, or honouring budget_tokens above the hard limit, would make the tools usable on a ledger this size.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.the-first-phase-25-work-proposal-was-rejected [about akr]
        The first Phase 25 work proposal was rejected because the work intent was supplied at the top level with an invalid topic slot; retrying with the documented slots.intent form succeeded.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.the-first-phase-26-diagnostic-harness-run
        The first Phase 26 diagnostic harness run resolved its repository root two levels too shallow and pointed at an obsolete input path. I corrected it to ../../.. and the pinned Phase 8 aggregate-instrumentation inputs before rerunning successfully.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.the-installed-akr-0-3-1-rejected-four-existing [about akr]
        The installed akr 0.3.1 rejected four existing observation records because it expected method instrumented, while current official AKR source accepts the documented method observation. A temporary build from official HEAD was required to read context, update evidence, and validate the ledger.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.the-repository-root-and-the-jpxl-crate-root-use [about cargo]
        The repository root and the JPXL crate root use different relative paths; two verification invocations initially targeted the release binary/input paths from the wrong root and failed with 'No such file or directory'. Running the same commands from JPXL with ../.agent paths resolved it.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.while-checking-an-in-progress-akr-change-akr [about akr]
        While checking an in-progress AKR change, `akr change status` was rejected because the CLI exposes `change show` instead; a status alias or help hint would make this transition easier to discover.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.while-repairing-phase-4l-evidence-chronology [about akr]
        While repairing Phase 4L evidence chronology, knowledge.revise returned the completed work revision to proposed even though the call explicitly passed state="completed". A follow-up knowledge.complete restored the intended terminal state; the tool documentation and project gotcha both say re-passing state should preserve it.

        ## orderflower @orderflower.papercut.akr-mcp-server-failed-to-connect-at-session [about akr]
        AKR MCP server failed to connect at session start, so knowledge.start/context were unavailable and I had to fall back to the akr CLI. Same pattern as a down integration rather than a workspace problem.

        ## orderflower @orderflower.papercut.knowledge-mcp-server-failed-to-connect-timed [about akr]
        knowledge.* MCP server failed to connect (timed out). Used the akr CLI instead; start/context still work, but the protocol's first-call path is the MCP tools.

        ## orderflower @orderflower.papercut.on-a-freshly-initialised-repo-with-no-commits [about akr]
        On a freshly initialised repo with no commits yet, knowledge.evidence_add and knowledge.papercut both fail with "no commit to record: not inside a git repository". That blocks knowledge.complete for every acceptance check at exactly the moment a first milestone finishes, and the message points at the wrong cause: git init had been run, there simply were no commits. A message naming the real fix (make an initial commit, or pass observed_at) would have saved a detour.

        ## orderflower @orderflower.papercut.orderflower-rithmic-record-uses-rithmic-rs
        orderflower-rithmic record uses rithmic-rs ConnectStrategy::Retry. Handshake timeout is 2s and Retry never stops, so a bad or slow plant prints nothing and hangs until killed. login --simple fails in about 2s.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.a-chained-focused-test-build-command-exceeded
        A chained focused-test/build command exceeded the executor's shortened timeout before producing results; verification must use separate commands with explicit longer limits.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.a-combined-read-only-akr-get-for-three-known
        A combined read-only akr get for three known records timed out before returning output; records must be queried separately or with a longer timeout.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.a-fresh-evidence-add-used-an-inferred-expansion
        A fresh evidence_add used an inferred expansion of the displayed short commit id and failed AKR-G011; the exact 40-character HEAD must be obtained with git rev-parse before setting observed_at.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.a-powershell-measure-object-call-using-a
        A PowerShell Measure-Object call using a calculated-property hashtable failed while extracting nested JSON metrics, requiring a retry with an explicit value array; nested summary analysis examples would avoid this small handoff friction.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.a-release-build-invocation-returned-without
        A release build invocation returned without Cargo's Finished line and left the previous binary in place, so the first batch gate rejected the new --lens-correction flag. Retrying the build explicitly and verifying --help before the batch; tooling should surface the subprocess exit status when output is handed off through a cell.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.a-targeted-cargo-test-invocation-with-two-exact [about cargo]
        A targeted `cargo test` invocation with two exact test filters fails because Cargo accepts only one positional filter; filtering on the containing `tone::tests` module is the reliable way to run both.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.a-two-frame-lens-correction-profile-exact
        A two-frame --lens-correction profile-exact render was killed after decode: the job-memory planner does not yet account for simultaneous RGB and clip-confidence resampling buffers. Retrying the diagnostic at --jobs 1 avoids the peak; the planner should budget profiled lens correction before this mode can graduate from opt-in.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.akr-check-passed-with-commit-none-before-commit
        akr check passed with commit (none) before commit, then failed six AKR-R022 temporal checks after commit because work records and their evidence first entered Git together; the workflow needs a pre-commit diagnostic for evidence that will predate newly committed work content.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.akr-explain-assessment-lists-optional-as-of-but [about akr]
        akr explain assessment lists optional as_of but not that it requires a git commit; using an ISO date caused a safe parse failure. Showing slot types in explain would avoid this retry.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.akr-get-shows-a-record-key-and-revision-but-not
        AKR get shows a record key and revision but not its source path or an exportable replacement body; locating the sealed head for akr revise --from required an extra filesystem layout check.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.akr-propose-from-rejected-a-prose-body-as-does [about akr]
        akr propose --from rejected a prose body as 'does not parse as a record'; the CLI help calls it a body source but this build requires a complete canonical record.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.akr-revise-from-help-describes-a-replacement
        akr revise --from help describes a replacement body, but a plain-text body fails AKR-C031 because the file must parse as a complete record; the required record wrapper is not shown in revise help.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.akr-search-prints-record-identifiers-with
        akr search prints record identifiers with revision suffixes (for example /2), but copying that identifier into the required akr context --goal call fails; context expects the unsuffixed key.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.akr-supersede-documented-with-a-replacement-key
        akr supersede documented --with a replacement key and the replacement had already been proposed, but the command still returned AKR-C004 saying different-key supersession is unsupported and repeated the already-satisfied proposal instruction.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.cargo-test-accepts-one-positional-testname
        Cargo test accepts one positional TESTNAME filter, so attempting to name two exact tests in one invocation fails before compilation; run the filters as separate commands.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.cargo-test-accepts-only-one-positional-test
        Cargo test accepts only one positional test-name filter; a focused verification command listing three test names was rejected and had to be split into separate invocations.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.fff-find-files-again-closed-its-transport-while
        FFF find_files again closed its transport while locating the requested review RAWs, forcing a filesystem fallback before a time-sensitive render run.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.fff-multi-grep-returned-transport-closed-while [about fff]
        FFF multi_grep returned 'Transport closed' while locating CLI and highlight pipeline symbols; falling back to rg as the repository instructions allow after tool failure.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.fff-multi-grep-still-closes-its-transport-when
        FFF multi_grep still closes its transport when searching the harmonic highlight code, so discovery again fell back to rg after the required FFF-first attempt.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.fff-multi-grep-transport-closed-while-locating [about fff]
        FFF multi_grep transport closed while locating the encoder-hints API across Rust sources, forcing a fallback to scoped rg/read.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.forwarding-six-full-resolution-diagnostic-pngs
        Forwarding six full-resolution diagnostic PNGs through the image viewer exceeded the IPC frame limit; making a downscaled montage first is required, but the limit is only reported after all images are loaded.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.grade-sky-py-reported-zero-pairs-on-a-normal
        `grade_sky.py` reported zero pairs on a normal recursive batch output because rendered files were nested under the input directory name; the tool does not recurse or point the user to the discovered child directory.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.i-tried-to-pass-several-exact-test-name-filters [about cargo]
        I tried to pass several exact test-name filters to one `cargo test` invocation; Cargo accepts only one positional TESTNAME filter, so the focused low-light tests had to be rerun using their shared module/name scope.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.imagemagick-compare-returns-exit-status-1-when
        ImageMagick compare returns exit status 1 when images differ even though it successfully reports RMSE; metric-only review commands need to tolerate that expected status.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.imagemagick-crop-review-composition-initially
        ImageMagick crop review composition initially put +append before its input images; the CLI reports no images found and requires the operator after the input list.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.knowledge-context-rejects-a-completed-work
        knowledge.context rejects a completed work record even when a follow-up scoping task needs its full history; the error does not suggest the nearest active related record.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.knowledge-explain-observation-and-knowledge [about akr]
        knowledge.explain observation and knowledge.papercut both failed with Transport closed while recording the sky-stage diagnosis; the local akr CLI worked as a fallback.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.knowledge-search-and-knowledge-start-via-the
        knowledge.search and knowledge.start via the akr MCP tool repeatedly failed with FTS5 errors (e.g. "fts5: syntax error near ','" on a comma-containing query, and "no such column: default" on the query 'HDR slice 6 non-default feature'). Queries with bare punctuation or reserved-looking words need escaping/quoting, or the tool should sanitise them. Fell back to grepping .akr/records directly.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.mcp-akr-tools-knowledge-search-knowledge
        MCP akr tools knowledge_search/knowledge_context returned 'unsupported call' from the akr MCP server (knowledge_start worked), so I fell back to the akr CLI. The two names may not be wired in this MCP build.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.naming-tools-scene-models-inspect-py-shadowed
        Naming tools/scene_models/inspect.py shadowed the stdlib inspect module: running prepare.py as a script put that directory on sys.path, so import onnx died inside typing_extensions. Renamed the script to report.py.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.pdftotext-poppler-not-installed-on-this-windows
        pdftotext/poppler not installed on this Windows host though AGENTS/user workflow assumes it; used Python PyMuPDF (fitz) to extract text and render equation pages instead.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.re-running-stage-dumps-into-an-explicit-tmp
        Re-running stage dumps into an explicit `/tmp` diagnostic directory was rejected because the command contained `rm -rf`; using a fresh `mktemp -d` directory avoids the cleanup and is safer.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.rtx-4060-wgpu-on-linux-is-currently-unusable
        RTX 4060 wgpu on Linux is currently unusable; scene inference stays on lege-gpu run_cpu. Added WGPU_PREFER_INTEGRATED and WGPU_ADAPTER_SKIP so a later GPU path can use the Intel iGPU and skip the 4060.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.running-several-read-only-akr-search-commands
        Running several read-only akr search commands concurrently caused one search to fail with AKR-I004 because .akr/cache/index.sqlite had no AKR meta table; AKR cache rebuild/search does not appear concurrency-safe.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.the-agents-protocol-names-knowledge-context-as
        The AGENTS protocol names knowledge.context as the first-step command, but that command is not available in the project shell; agents must infer/use the akr CLI equivalent.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.the-akr-cli-search-syntax-differs-from-the-mcp [about akr]
        The AKR CLI search syntax differs from the MCP shape: --query is rejected and the help must be consulted separately.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.the-corpus-smoke-command-combined-summary-file
        The corpus smoke command combined --summary FILE with --no-summary; clap correctly rejected the mutually exclusive flags after a long release link. The CLI error is clear, but running argument validation before release compilation would make this iteration cheaper.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.the-first-focused-cargo-test-invocation-passed
        The first focused cargo test invocation passed two positional test filters, which Cargo rejects; reran with the shared module filter.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.the-first-focused-release-test-compile-exceeded
        The first focused release test compile exceeded a 60-second timeout; this workspace needs a multi-minute timeout for cold optimized test linking.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.the-first-standalone-python-regression-test
        The first standalone Python regression test imported its sibling as a top-level module, but unittest discovery runs from the repository root and omits tools/ from sys.path; load the script by its explicit file path so either invocation works.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.the-full-batch-process-stopped-at-the-execution
        The full batch process stopped at the execution harness's ~30-second lifetime, initially resembling another OOM. Inspection found 28 images already written incrementally and no surviving process; bounded restart with skip-existing is required for long validation runs in this environment.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.the-jobs-8-determinism-harness-used-get
        The jobs-8 determinism harness used Get-ChildItem -Include on a literal directory path and silently matched zero files, producing a vacuous success until the hash count was checked; use an explicit extension filter or wildcard path.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.the-knowledge-context-mcp-connector-returned [about akr]
        The knowledge.context MCP connector returned 'Transport closed' at the start of implementation; using the equivalent akr CLI workflow.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.the-low-light-analysis-only-pass-used-highlight
        The low-light analysis-only pass used `--highlight-reconstruction 0`, but validation rejected it because the default harmonic method requires strength 1 even though reconstruction was disabled. The workaround is the non-obvious pair `--highlight-method current --highlight-reconstruction 0`; zero strength could plausibly bypass the method constraint.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.the-reconstruction-off-ablation-was-initially [about raw-autotune CLI]
        The reconstruction-off ablation was initially rejected because the automatic harmonic method requires full reconstruction strength. The compatible disabled control is `--highlight-method current --highlight-reconstruction 0`; the CLI help/validation could make this pairing more discoverable.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.the-unit-tests-that-pinned-the-da23c5f-near
        The unit tests that pinned the da23c5f near-white anchor rule were kept by name and docstring while their bodies were relaxed to weaker claims (exact channel equality became "spread should not grow much"; a test named near_white_reconstruction_is_independent_of_strength gained a comment saying near-white pixels now do vary with strength). The suite stayed green through a visible rendering regression. Worth a convention: when a rewrite makes a pinned invariant false, delete the test and say so in the changelog rather than editing its body under its old name.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.updating-a-decision-record-initially-failed
        Updating a decision record initially failed with AKR-T001 because its prose slot is named decision rather than statement; the retry required changing the typed body after consulting the diagnostic.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.while-auditing-low-light-false-positives-dry
        While auditing low-light false positives, --dry-run still ran harmonic highlight transport and other downstream processing even though only AnalysisStats was needed; the 376-frame pass projected to roughly 15 minutes and had to be replaced with summary-led sampling. A detector/analysis-only fast path would make controller calibration much cheaper.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.while-locating-hdr-sky-local-tone-and [about FFF]
        While locating HDR, sky, local-tone, and evaluation files, a parallel batch of FFF find_files calls all failed with `Transport closed`; retrying with a single narrow request.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.while-locating-the-archived-dsc1289-source-fff [about FFF]
        While locating the archived _DSC1289 source, FFF returned many generated renders but not the ignored raw/raw_3rd_batch/_DSC1289.ARW file, so discovery had to fall back to a bounded filesystem find. Showing ignored in-workspace exact-name matches would make archive gates easier to reproduce.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.while-proposing-the-follow-on-work-record-a [about akr]
        While proposing the follow-on work record, a dense inline MCP payload produced an unhelpful JavaScript syntax error before the AKR call ran; compact payload examples or earlier argument validation would make retries easier.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.while-recording-the-visual-rejection-two-apply
        While recording the visual rejection, two apply_patch contexts missed because the nearby changelog text differed from the expected wording; the exact section had to be re-read before retrying with a minimal anchor.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.while-running-the-focused-scene-and-preview [about cargo]
        While running the focused scene and preview tests, `cargo test` rejected two positional test filters; Cargo accepts only one filter, so the validation had to be rerun with a single shared filter or as separate invocations.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.while-running-three-targeted-rust-tests-i
        While running three targeted Rust tests I passed multiple test filters to one cargo test invocation; Cargo accepts only one positional filter. Retried with a shared substring/full suite; an error hint mentioning this limitation would reduce the small loop.
        """
    observed_at git:1d6defbf53ad70aa869a547c7c58aeb61141176f
