record lege-ecosystem.papercut.creating-the-publication-work-record-first/1 : papercut {
    title "Creating the publication work record first failed because work requires…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Creating the publication work record first failed because work requires an intent slot and rejects topic; the schema requirements were only disclosed after the write attempt.
        """
    observed_at git:3f520cc03211e48adaa77c1da9bc639c53d2d351
    about "akr"
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-23
}

record lege-ecosystem.papercut.during-packaging-inventory-an-rg-filter-whose/1 : papercut {
    title "During packaging inventory, an rg filter whose pattern began with…"
    state verified
    statement """
        During packaging inventory, an rg filter whose pattern began with `-sys` was parsed as a flag, and Windows wildcard path arguments such as `crates/*/Cargo.toml` were not expanded. Retrying with `--` and rg-native `-g` globs is required in PowerShell.
        """
    observed_at git:1d6defbf53ad70aa869a547c7c58aeb61141176f
    about "ripgrep"
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-15
}

record lege-ecosystem.papercut.eagerly-creating-and-tearing-down-a-winrt/1 : papercut {
    title "Eagerly creating and tearing down a WinRT OcrEngine during backend…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Eagerly creating and tearing down a WinRT OcrEngine during backend initialization completed normally in the release CLI but crashed the longer-lived Rust test process at teardown with STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION. WinOCR initialization must remain lazy or use a lifecycle-safe dedicated apartment rather than a short-lived preflight object.
        """
    observed_at git:1d6defbf53ad70aa869a547c7c58aeb61141176f
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-15
}

record lege-ecosystem.papercut.evidence-records-routinely-cite-agent-scratch/1 : papercut {
    title "Evidence records routinely cite `.agent/scratch` paths as their…"
    state superseded
    statement """
        Evidence records routinely cite `.agent/scratch` paths as their `artifact`, but scratch is documented as prunable and nothing in the ledger protects a cited path: 38 records across 5 .akr files reference `.agent/scratch/...`. Most are already dangling — when `.agent/scratch/ocr-benchmark` was inspected on 2026-08-22 it held only score.py, b3.*, target/ and three recipe output dirs, while eight separate evidence records cite sibling paths under it (tensorrt-smoke-*, lazy-corrected-*, out-winocr-12mp-200-sharded, release-auto-winocr-*, release-tensorrt-*, turboocr-*.txt) that had already been deleted. So verified claims silently lose their backing. Either `akr build`/`validate` should warn when an artifact path is under the scratch root or has vanished, or `knowledge.evidence_add` should refuse a scratch-relative artifact and tell the author to move it somewhere durable first.
        """
    observed_at git:3f520cc03211e48adaa77c1da9bc639c53d2d351
    about "akr"
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-22
}

record lege-ecosystem.papercut.evidence-records-routinely-cite-agent-scratch/2 : papercut {
    title "Evidence records routinely cite `.agent/scratch` paths as their…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Evidence records routinely cite `.agent/scratch` paths as their `artifact`, but scratch is documented as prunable and nothing stops a cited path being deleted: 38 records across 5 .akr files reference `.agent/scratch/...`. Most are already dangling — when `.agent/scratch/ocr-benchmark` was inspected on 2026-08-22 it held only score.py, b3.*, target/ and three recipe output dirs, while eight separate evidence records cite sibling paths under it (tensorrt-smoke-*, lazy-corrected-*, out-winocr-12mp-200-sharded, release-auto-winocr-*, release-tensorrt-*, turboocr-*.txt) that had already been pruned. Those verified claims silently lost their backing. The fix belongs in `knowledge.evidence_add`: it should refuse an `artifact` path under the scratch root outright, at write time, and tell the author to move the artefact somewhere durable first. Refusing at the point of writing is what makes the guarantee hold — a warning emitted later by `akr build` or `validate` arrives after the record is already in the ledger, and by then the usual outcome is a dangling reference nobody re-reads. A durable-path precondition is cheap to check and turns an unenforced convention into an invariant.
        """
    observed_at git:3f520cc03211e48adaa77c1da9bc639c53d2d351
    about "akr"
    supersedes [ @lege-ecosystem.papercut.evidence-records-routinely-cite-agent-scratch/1 ]
}

